From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dix: room for ten events from one input, not a hundred

Every event list the server keeps, the input queue's and XTEST's among
them, holds GetMaximumEventsNum() InternalEvents of 2.6 KB each: 256 KB a
list at 100.  With an MMU the untouched pages cost nothing; without one
each list is 256 KB of RAM.  An input makes at most a raw event, the event
and a device-changed event, plus scroll-button emulation, which stops at
whatever room is left.  Ten keeps room for three scroll steps at once, and
the WikiReader's touch screen and buttons have no scroll axes.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: N/A sized for a machine without an MMU
---
 dix/getevents.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/dix/getevents.c
+++ b/dix/getevents.c
@@ -647,10 +647,10 @@
     /* One raw event
      * One device event
      * One possible device changed event
-     * Lots of possible separate button scroll events (horiz + vert)
-     * Lots of possible separate raw button scroll events (horiz + vert)
+     * A few separate button scroll events (horiz + vert), which
+     * emulate_scroll_button_events stops at this limit
      */
-    return 100;
+    return 10;
 }
 
